<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">May Coup (Poland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1926</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The May Coup was the seizure of power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> by Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozef-pilsudski">Józef Piłsudski</a> from 12 to 14 May 1926. After fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> that killed several hundred people, the government and president resigned. Piłsudski then dominated the Second Polish Republic until his death in 1935 through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanation">Sanation</a> regime, which kept parliament but weakened it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/may-coup-poland.jpg" alt="May Coup (Poland)" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marian Fuks (1884-1935) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pi%C5%82sudski_May_1926.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
